  52:Source/render/decoders/webp.c ****  * Lua parity notes:
  53:Source/render/decoders/webp.c ****  *  - data:byte(pos) is 1-based; pos == len+1 reads nil in Lua → the loop
  54:Source/render/decoders/webp.c ****  *    condition `pos <= br.len` gives one extra iteration reading past the
  55:Source/render/decoders/webp.c ****  *    last real byte? No: Lua's data:byte(len+1) returns nil and `|` would
  56:Source/render/decoders/webp.c ****  *    error — the reference relies on the while condition ending at pos>len.
  57:Source/render/decoders/webp.c ****  *    The final iteration uses pos == len (the last real byte); after that
  58:Source/render/decoders/webp.c ****  *    pos = len+1 stops the loop. So window fills from real bytes only.
  59:Source/render/decoders/webp.c ****  *  - eos latches once and is never cleared by brAdvance/readBits. */
  60:Source/render/decoders/webp.c **** void webp_br_init(WebPBitReader *br, const uint8_t *data, int len, int startPos)
