 158:Source/render/decoders/webp.c **** 
 159:Source/render/decoders/webp.c **** /* replicateValue: table[base+i*step] = code for i = end/step-1 .. 0.
 160:Source/render/decoders/webp.c ****  * Lua uses 1-based table indices via base+currentEnd; here the table is a
 161:Source/render/decoders/webp.c ****  * plain C array and base/currentEnd are 0-based entry indices. The Lua code
 162:Source/render/decoders/webp.c ****  * indexes table[base + currentEnd] where currentEnd counts down by step —
 163:Source/render/decoders/webp.c ****  * with Lua 1-based tables this writes entries base+end-step .. base+1... the
